# Pinned upstream versions of the vendored webterm web assets (see update.sh).
#
# These files are checked in and inlined into the webterm page (features.Script),
# so the page is fully offline and reproducible — there is no runtime download.
# To bump: edit a version here, run ./update.sh, verify the page still works,
# and commit versions.env + the asset(s) + SHA256SUMS together.
#
# Held at 5.5.0 on purpose (checked 2026-07). xterm 6.0.0's core is actually
# API-compatible — its UMD still exposes globalThis.Terminal / FitAddon.FitAddon
# and every method this page uses is intact — BUT @xterm/addon-fit has no stable
# release for xterm 6: `latest` is 0.11.0 with peer @xterm/xterm@^5.0.0, and only
# 0.12.0-beta.* pairs with 6.x. Taking 6.0.0 would mean vendoring a beta addon (or
# dropping the addon for private-internals sizing), which defeats the point of
# pinning. Revisit when addon-fit ships a stable 0.12.x for xterm 6, and confirm
# the page in a real mobile browser (fit + /ws) before switching the default.
XTERM_VERSION=5.5.0
XTERM_ADDON_FIT_VERSION=0.10.0
